### 4.1 WHEN to Activate

After the Goal Contract is constructed and before choosing an execution strategy.

### 4.2 WHAT to Estimate

| Dimension | Scale |
|---|---|
| `COMPLEXITY` | Trivial → Simple → Moderate → Complex → Very Complex |
| `UNCERTAINTY` | None → Low → Medium → High → Extreme |
| `SCOPE` | Single file → Multiple files → Multiple modules → Full system |
| `DEPENDENCIES` | None → Few → Many → Interdependent → Circular risk |
| `RESEARCH_DEPTH` | None → Quick check → Substantial → Deep investigation |
| `TOOL_REQUIREMENTS` | Basic → Standard → Specialized → Unavailable (must improvise) |
| `PARALLELISM_OPPORTUNITY` | None → Low → Medium → High |
| `RISK` | Minimal → Low → Medium → High → Critical |
| `VERIFICATION_DIFFICULTY` | Trivial → Easy → Moderate → Difficult → Requires independent testing |
| `EXPECTED_COST` | Single step → Few steps → Multiple rounds → Extensive |

### 4.3 HOW to Choose Strategy

**SIMPLE TASK:**
UNDERSTAND → EXECUTE → VERIFY → STOP

