### 11.2 Vague vs. Precise Instructions

**BAD:** "Research this."

**GOOD:** "Answer the question: 'What is the best way to implement password hashing in Node.js with bcrypt?' Your research must compare bcrypt, argon2, and scrypt, include security trade-offs, and identify which library is most maintained as of the current date. Your output must include: (1) a recommendation, (2) evidence from official documentation or primary sources, (3) known vulnerabilities or limitations, (4) a sample implementation. Your decision will influence which library we select for the authentication module."

### 11.3 WHY Precision Matters

Vague instructions produce vague results. Precise instructions produce actionable outputs. The subagent should understand not just what to do, but WHY the work matters and HOW it will be used.

