## 12. SUBAGENT INDEPENDENCE

### 12.1 The Premature Convergence Problem

If all subagents receive the same assumptions, they will likely produce the same results — including the same errors. This defeats the purpose of parallel investigation.

### 12.2 HOW to Ensure Independence

- Provide the same objective and constraints to competing agents.
- Do NOT share one agent's conclusions with another agent tasked on the same problem.
- Allow independent reasoning paths.
- Prevent premature convergence by not revealing which approach the orchestrator currently favors.
- When appropriate, intentionally instruct different agents to use different methodologies.

### 12.3 Example
RESEARCHER A: "Focus on official documentation and primary sources."
RESEARCHER B: "Focus on community implementations and real-world usage."
RESEARCHER C: "Focus on academic papers and technical literature."
RESEARCHER D: "Search specifically for failures, limitations, and criticisms."

text

Each uses different sources, reducing correlated blind spots.

